  "brief_rationale": "The doctor correctly assessed respiratory danger (RC1), interpreted the CT result as requiring inpatient respiratory care (RC2), gathered key vitals/diagnoses and acknowledged unknowns (RC3), bounded medication safety without endorsing self-adjustment (RC4), and provided a transfer/handoff plan (RC5). All responsibility-chain items were met without serious or minor error. The closure remained a valid open episode; the doctor gave clear next steps and the family confirmed understanding. Two case-defined high-order points were fully triggered and completed with active model actions: HO1 (correcting the misconception that 'no fever/SpO2 97% means safe') and HO4 (adapting the plan to the family's real-world constraints during transfer). The trajectory therefore achieves Strong, and because two HO points were completed with meaningful impact it meets the strict criteria for Perfect (grade 5).",
